<!-- Petoi Bittle X — MuJoCo MJCF for MH-FLOCKE
     SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the Bittle BODY.
     Synced 2026-06-08 from the published, menagerie-quality model
       github.com/MarcHesse/bittle-mujoco

     Mass validation (2026-06-08, physically weighed, Bittle X V1 / BiBoard V0_1):
       Total with battery:   273.5 g  (Petoi spec: 265-290 g) ✓
       Battery (LiPo):        55.0 g
       Head + neck servo:     18.7 g
       One P1S servo:         10.7 g  (shoulder x4, knee x4, neck x1)
       One complete leg:      20.0 g  (thigh bracket + knee servo + shank)
       Lower leg + servo:     14.0 g  → shank bracket alone: 3.3 g
       Torso frame (derived): 77.0 g  (total - battery - head - 4x leg)
       Visual-only bodies:    ~0.0 g  (mass=1e-6 kg each, negligible)

     Foot sites corrected (2026-06-08): FK-derived, z=0 at stand pose.
     Sites placed in servos_rf/rr/lf/lr bodies (not shank) to match weld group.
     NOTE: MuJoCo 3.5.0 touch sensor bug — rf/lf/rr/lr_contact always reads 0.
     Root cause: efc_force scaling changed in MuJoCo 3.x; touch sensor not updated.
     Workaround: use mj_contactForce() + data.ncon in Python for contact detection.
     Track: github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/issues (open bug)

     MH-FLOCKE instrumentation carried in this model (used by train_baby / render):
       - imu_site + 4 foot sites (rf/lf/rr/lr_foot_site)
       - full <sensor> block (IMU accel/gyro/quat + framepos/velocimeter + 8 jointpos + 4 touch)
       - <keyframe name="stand"> (train_baby auto-reset via mj_resetDataKeyframe)
       - root body "torso", materials

     8 position actuators, MH-FLOCKE order:
       0: rf_shoulder (shrfs_joint)   1: rf_knee (shrft_joint)
       2: lf_shoulder (shlfs_joint)   3: lf_knee (shlft_joint)
       4: rr_shoulder (shrrs_joint)   5: rr_knee (shrrt_joint)
       6: lr_shoulder (shlrs_joint)   7: lr_knee (shlrt_joint)
     Note: neck_joint exists but is not actuated.
     NOTE: brain input stays IMU + proprioception + CPG only (#59); framepos/
     velocimeter/touch are sim-only trainer ground-truth, never fed to the SNN.
-->
